## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Hai: Standup

> *"Today I moved email out of the request path and into a job queue.*
> *I'm using pg-boss, which runs on Postgres rather than Redis. I already have Postgres, and adding Redis means adding something else that can go down. But there's a better reason: because the queue lives in the same database, I can enqueue a job inside a transaction. If the transaction rolls back, the job disappears with it. With a Redis queue you can have the database write fail and the email still go out.*
> *The part I spent most time on was retries. Exponential backoff, because retrying immediately against an overloaded provider makes the outage worse. And a hard rule: don't retry what can never succeed. A malformed email address will still be malformed on the fifth attempt — that goes straight to the dead letter queue.*
> *Jobs also have to be idempotent, because a process can die after sending the email but before marking the job done. That's the third place this month I've had to make an operation safe to run twice — offline writes, push receipts, and now background jobs. Same idea each time."*

Câu cuối là câu mạnh nhất. Nhận ra một khuôn mẫu lặp lại là dấu hiệu của người hiểu, không phải người thuộc.

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `the request path` | đường đi của request | *I moved email out of the request path.* |
| `roll back` | quay lui giao dịch | *If the transaction rolls back, the job disappears.* |
| `make the outage worse` | làm sự cố tệ hơn | *Retrying immediately makes the outage worse.* |
| `dead letter queue` | hàng đợi chết | *That goes straight to the dead letter queue.* |
| `safe to run twice` | chạy hai lần vẫn an toàn | *Make the operation safe to run twice.* |

